  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Features**\n\nI\'ve been mapping out the project\'s core components. I\'m focusing on user management, exploring how registration, logins, and access controls will work. The plan includes detailed user profiles and robust role-based access. I\'m also considering team invites and related features.\n\n\n**Defining System Elements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the finer details. I\'m building out modules for project management with creation, editing, archiving, and status tracking. Team management is next, covering member directories, collaboration, and feedback. Task and workflow management with kanban boards, and milestone tracking are in progress, and I am exploring the fair contribution analysis elements to ensure accurate project completion.\n\n\n**Developing Advanced Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating sophisticated AI features. I\'m focusing on scoring, incorporating task complexity and quality assessment. Role-aware scoring and contribution confidence are central, with missing evidence detection for transparency. I\'m also including detailed contribution history and score explanations for dispute resolution. Finally, I\'m integrating recognition of invisible work to ensure fair contribution, while working on the team\'s workload.\n\n\n**Expanding System Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating AI-powered features like smart task recommendations and meeting summary generation, including stand-up generators and AI-driven action items. I am including simulation and project recovery elements, with what-if simulators and deadline impact analysis. I\'m also planning learning and continuous improvement tools, like estimation accuracy analysis and retrospective insights. Furthermore, I\'m working on dashboards, reports, notifications, communication, and integrations.\n\n\n**Evaluating Feature Set**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a direct comparison, scrutinizing existing functionalities against the requested additions. I\'m prioritizing security and privacy features like authentication, authorization, and audit logs. I\'m assessing multi-language support, custom contribution weights, and AI project planning, and the skill check has concluded that frontend-design is relevant.\n\n\n"
