  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Server Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing `server.ts` to map out routes and database tables. I\'ve noted the `projects` table details like objectives, dates, status, and leadership. I see team management data, user authentication, and data retrieval processes are included. I\'m focusing on how these interact to form core functionality, especially regarding project tracking.\n\n\n**Mapping Database Relationships**\n\nI\'ve been examining the table schemas, specifically focusing on the relationships between `members`, `project_members`, and the task-related tables. The connections are crucial for understanding member roles within projects and how task assignments and reviews are managed. I am now looking at how tasks are linked to Github activity, and audit logging.\n\n\n**Evaluating Feature Integration**\n\nI\'m now comparing the system\'s current features against the 18 requirements. Authentication is set, with registration, login, and user roles in place. The `project_invitations` table seems to facilitate team invitations, that\'s good. Password reset functionality is missing an endpoint and UI, and user profile management (avatar, bio, Github username, password) requires attention. I\'m noting the need for a modal for password resets.\n\n\n**Refining UI Implementations**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the user interface elements related to project and team management. There\'s a need to build an invitation UI to handle sending and viewing invitations, including token and role management. Also, I\'m working on permissions and role-based access control, plus session management considerations.\n\n\n**Expanding Collaboration Features**\n\nI\'m now investigating file attachments, thinking we need file sharing for tasks and projects, potentially as a mock. Good news \342\200\223 a `meeting_notes` table is already there! I\'m planning to build a dedicated Collaboration tab to showcase meeting notes with action items and attendees. Blocker reporting functionality is present! Also, a dedicated channel for team discussions is needed. I\'m focusing on tasks, subtasks, assignment, priorities, deadlines, status, and Kanban, and am planning Calendar and Timeline/Gantt views too.\n\n\n**Assessing Collaborative Tools**\n\nI\'m now integrating Acceptance Criteria and Task Reviews within the `JiraIssueDetailModal`. I see the risk engine already handles deadline reminders and critical path calculations, which I\'m planning on adding interactive UI components for. Additionally, I\'m focusing on ensuring robust contribution categorizes task types like `Story` and `Bug` and others.\n\n\n**Developing Contribution Analyses**\n\nI\'m now focusing on contribution analysis, specifically integrating evidence-based scoring, task complexity weighting, and role-aware scoring within the interface. I\'m ensuring missing evidence detection and dispute resolution functionalities are interactive, too. I\'m keen to make the \'Disputes\' modal and missing evidence dashboard visible within the `ContributionsPage`.\nI\'m also working on workload and skill distribution, checking capacity hours in the DB and seeing how overload, under-allocation, and skill-aware task matching are being handled. I plan on providing a \"Smart Task Redistribution\" UI component, with a button to suggest task reassignments!\n\n\n**Implementing Project Health**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the project health analytics, and planning to generate a composite \"Health Score\" (0-100) based on on-time delivery, blocker count, risk score, and test coverage. This will be visible in both the `DashboardPage` and `ProjectsPage` as a health score card and comparisons of planned vs actual progress. I\'m also planning to flag members who are the sole assignees of critical path items to mitigate knowledge dependencies.\n\n\n**Planning AI Assistant Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating new AI features. I\'m adding action buttons like \"Generate Daily Standup\" and \"Draft Sprint Retro\" in the `AIAssistantDrawer`, along with other actions. I\'m also planning to build a \"Simulation & Recovery View/Modal\" for what-if scenarios and recovery planning. I\'m focusing on features such as deadline impact analysis.\n\n\n**Adding Retrospective Reporting**\n\nI\'m now implementing a new \"Sprint Retrospectives\" view to capture \"What went well\", \"Needs Improvement\", and related action items. Additionally, I\'m integrating decision-to-outcome tracking within this view. Furthermore, I am planning three different dashboard views (Project Manager, Team Member, and Admin) to provide role-specific insights.\nI am also adding a workload heatmap, a risk dashboard, and a collaboration graph. I\'m exploring adding a printable PDF/CSV formatted executive report.\nFinally, I\'m focused on the in-app notification center alerts for overdue tasks and more, and integrations with email and calendar are also in scope.\n\n\n"
