  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Registration**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on the requested user and access management features. Registration, as a starting point, is already in place. My immediate concern is establishing the proper framework for a complete user access system based on a detailed breakdown.\n\n\n**Developing User Authentication**\n\nI\'ve been working on integrating login functionality and user profile management, which will be visible in the authentication and top bar components. Role-based access control, with roles like Admin, Manager, Member, and Project Director, is in development. Session token management is also underway. Next up are database schema and endpoints for Team Invitations. I have yet to address password resets, a dedicated user profile editor, or the Team Invitations UI. I also plan to visualize a role permissions matrix.\n\nI am now proceeding to the project management modules. The ability to create, edit, add start/end dates, assign project status, and objectives in the database, has already been completed. I now plan to integrate project archiving with an associated UI and filter, and a project priority field.\n\n\n**Expanding Project Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now focused on enhancing project features. I\'m prioritizing the development of project templates, like Agile Sprint or Microservice API, for quick project setup with pre-populated tasks and milestones. Additionally, I\'m working on a project activity history viewer to track all changes with timestamps.\n\n\n**Refining Project Task Views**\n\nI\'m now diving into specific project task management features. I\'ve been considering subtasks, task assignments, and priority setting, as well as deadlines and status tracking. I plan to build out the Kanban board, backlog view, and list view. For each task I also plan to add acceptance criteria and support task reviews, incorporating drag-and-drop functionality. I still need to integrate calendar and timeline views, and I need to incorporate a visual task dependency selector.\n\n\n**Evaluating Contribution Features**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing contribution tracking and dispute resolution. I\'ve already implemented individual and team contribution scores and established the structure for task completion evidence and GitHub activity integration. My current focus is refining this with a multi-type contribution breakdown encompassing testing, bug fixes, code, and more, complete with \"Invisible Work\" badges. I\'ll need an interactive dispute resolution UI and a widget for missing evidence alerts. I\'m also planning to build a \"Smart Task Redistribution\" panel.\n\n\n**Assessing Project Health**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on project health analytics. I\'m focusing on the project scorecard, which will include on-time pacing, a blocker index, and a quality review rate, among other aspects. I\'m also planning a ripple effect simulator to model delays. I\'m also preparing a single-point-of-failure detector to identify dependency bottlenecks.\n\n\n**Planning Recovery & Improvement**\n\nI\'m now integrating an interactive \"What-If Simulator & Project Recovery Planner.\" It will have sliders to adjust deadlines and toggle member availability. I\'m also planning to build an automated recovery plan generator that will prioritize high ROI tasks, descope low-priority items, and reassign blocked tasks. Also planned are a Retrospectives UI tab for viewing and submitting sprint retrospectives and an Estimation Accuracy Dashboard to display planned vs actual hours.\n\n\n**Prioritizing User Roles**\n\nI\'m now implementing role-specific dashboards, including Project Manager, Team Member (\"My Tasks\", \"My Overdue\", \"My Reviews\"), and Admin views. I am also working on adding a Workload Heatmap grid and a Print/Formatted Executive PDF/Report View.\n\n\\n\\n\nI\'m also working on enhancements to the notification system, I plan to add filters, reminder triggers, and quick action links. Also on my list are calendar integration for project deadlines and task milestones, an email template/share link generator, and I\'ll need to create an audit log.\n\n\n**Adding System Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now focusing on system-level enhancements. I\'m adding a Logs Viewer tab to view audit history and a database backup/export function for data management. Furthermore, I\'ll be creating a Role Permissions & Security Matrix viewer. I am planning to implement advanced features like a configurable custom contribution weights, and also include a predictive deadline forecasting indicator.\n\n\n**Integrating New Sidebar Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating \'collaboration\' and \'simulation\' items into the sidebar navigation, making the UI more discoverable. I\'m also inspecting `server.ts` to verify existing API endpoints for meeting notes, retrospectives, disputes, audit logs, and project invitations, which seem to be missing. I need to get this added quickly.\n\n\n"
