  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Feature Integration**\n\nI\'m currently focused on ensuring all 18 feature domains integrate comprehensively. My review is underway, starting with user and access management; noting existing features like registration and login. I\'m taking a deep dive into the API requirements, starting with password reset functionality. I\'m aiming for seamless backend-UI usability across all these domains.\n\n\n**Expanding Feature Scope**\n\nI\'ve expanded the feature integration review to encompass user profiles, role-based access, and team invitations. Specifically, I\'m thinking through the integration points between these components, such as how user profiles connect to roles and how team invitations align with access controls. The focus is on API endpoints and corresponding UI elements. I\'m also planning project management features, including project archiving, objectives, templates, and activity history. Finally, I\'m integrating Team Management features like a member directory, task comments, meeting notes.\n\n\n**Integrating Task Visualizations**\n\nI\'m now integrating new task management visualizations. I\'m focusing on the calendar view, showing tasks on their due dates with priority tags, and the timeline/Gantt view, illustrating sprint dates, start and finish dates, and dependency arrows. I\'m also adding task dependencies with warnings. My current focus is to ensure these new visualizations seamlessly integrate with the existing task features.\n\n\n**Integrating New Task Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating new task-related features. I am currently focused on visualizing the Schedule Variance visualizer, showing the critical path and schedule buffer days, which already exist within project management intelligence. Additionally, I am designing an Overdue Task Detection & Reminders system. I\'m aiming to smoothly integrate these capabilities into the existing project structure. I\'m also developing both Contribution Tracking and Fair Contribution Analysis, including contribution scores, evidence tracking, and a category breakdown, and dispute resolution. Team workload and Skills features are also in the works. Finally, Project Health Analytics and Risk Intelligence are being added.\n\n\n**Adding New Features**\n\nI am now integrating the Ripple Effect & Bottleneck Simulator, an interactive slider to visualize delays. I\'m also adding Quick Action Prompts, like \"Generate Daily Standup,\" using the AI Assistant. I\'m actively working on the Interactive What-If Simulator & Recovery Planner. Furthermore, I\'m integrating Sprint Retrospectives UI and Estimation Accuracy Analysis charts for continuous improvement. Finally, I\'m adding role-based dashboards and workload heatmaps, along with export options, and a notification center.\n\n\n**Adding Endpoint Security**\n\nI\'m now integrating new endpoints for increased functionality and security. I\'ve focused on adding `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/profile`, `/api/invitations`, and `/api/discussions`, as well as their related backend functions in `server.ts`. This includes their respective GET and POST methods, with parameters such as email, passwords, and project IDs, while also checking audit logs.\n\n\n"
