    thinking: "**Defining Database Structure**\n\nI\'ve been working on defining the database schema within `server.ts`, focusing particularly on the `discussions` table. I\'m aiming for a straightforward structure with a primary key, `project_id`, author details, and a default category. I\'ve also incorporated error handling around table creation for robustness.\n\n\n**Adding API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now integrating new API endpoints into `server.ts`. I\'ve started with the `/api/auth/reset-password` endpoint, including validation for the email and password, and implemented a basic user lookup. I\'m focusing on ensuring proper error handling and response codes are used for a reliable API.\n\n\n**Implementing User Profile Updates**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `/api/auth/profile` endpoint, prioritizing authenticated user profile updates within `server.ts`. I\'m handling updates for name, avatar, GitHub username, and role, while also adding the capability to handle password updates. I am focusing on input validation and applying the appropriate query, and incorporating robust error handling. The endpoint should respond with appropriate status codes to indicate success or failure.\n\n\n**Refining Profile Endpoint**\n\nI\'ve just added the logic for the `/api/auth/profile` endpoint\'s update functionality, and I\'ve integrated input validation to ensure data integrity, including password updates. I\'ve also incorporated error handling for SQL queries and response codes, ensuring a reliable user profile update flow. This includes updating the `team_members` table if the emails or user ids match. The response will include the updated user object.\n\n\n**Adding Invitation API**\n\nI\'m currently working on the `/api/invitations` API endpoint. I\'ve implemented a GET request to fetch invitations with optional filtering by `project_id`. The POST request handles creating new invitations with email validation, a unique ID generation (`inv-`), a token, and setting an expiration date. I am also incorporating audit logging for each invitation created.\n\n\n**Developing Discussion API**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `/api/discussions` endpoint in `server.ts`. I have added a GET request to fetch discussions, with optional filtering by `project_id`, and sorting by creation date. The POST request handles creating new discussions, including validation for title and content. I\'m also using the auth user\'s data for the author fields, and auto-generating an `id` using the current timestamp. The response includes the new discussion details.\n\n\n**Finalizing Discussion Creation**\n\nI\'ve just finalized the implementation for the `/api/discussions` endpoint\'s POST request. I\'ve focused on generating a unique discussion `id` and integrating user data for author information, along with setting default values for the optional data. I also added a notification system, and I\'m ensuring the response provides the newly created discussion details. I\'m now moving on to the `/api/kudos` endpoint to continue development.\n\n\n**Implementing Kudos Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `/api/kudos` endpoint within `server.ts`. I have added a GET request that fetches kudos, with optional filtering by `project_id`. The POST request handles creating new kudos. I am incorporating validation for recipient member and message, generating a unique `id`, including the auth user\'s name for the `from_name` field, and setting a default category. I am ensuring that the `created_at` timestamp is correctly formatted.\n\n\n**Adding Audit Log API**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `/api/audit-logs` endpoint. It features a GET request to fetch audit logs, supporting optional filtering by `project_id`. The results are ordered by creation date and limited to the most recent 50 entries, and incorporates error handling. I\'m focusing on ensuring data integrity in the responses.\n\n\n\n**Updating Project Status**\n\nI\'ve just added the `/api/projects/:id/archive` endpoint. I\'m focusing on updating the project\'s archived status in the database based on the request body. I\'m also generating appropriate audit logs to track the changes, including who made them and what they were. I am validating the project exists, and returning the updated project with the response.\n\n\n**Refining Task Assignment**\n\nI\'ve just added the `/api/tasks/:id/assign` endpoint, focusing on reassigning tasks to balance workloads using Smart Redistribution. I\'m validating tasks and team members, and generating audit logs and notifications, including the assignee, task, and a relevant message. The update query and notifications are correctly structured now.\n\n\n**Implementing Database Backup**\n\nI\'m now creating a `/api/db/backup` endpoint in `server.ts` to implement a database backup. I\'m querying all tables for a full dump of the database and returning it as a JSON file. The response sets content headers for a download. I\'m ensuring everything is correctly formatted in JSON and offered to download.\n\n\n"
