  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Database Schema**\n\nI\'ve been working on defining the database schema in `server.ts`. I\'m starting by creating a `discussions` table. I\'m thinking of how I can best structure the data, including primary keys and the different types of author-related data I need. I\'m also considering what data types I need to incorporate.\n\n\n**Expanding Database Schema**\n\nI\'ve added tables for `peer_kudos` and `system_settings` to the database schema. I\'ve included data types and primary keys. I\'m also preparing sample seed data for the `discussions` and `peer_kudos` tables.\n\nNow I\'m looking at the UI views, and planning updates to User & Access Management, including a Forgot Password/Reset flow in `AuthModal.tsx`, profile updates in `UserProfileModal.tsx`, invitation management in `TeamInvitationsModal.tsx`, and role permission comparison in `RolePermissionsModal.tsx`.\n\n\n**Visualizing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the UI components. I\'m building out a matrix to map Role-Based Access Control permissions for different areas: Projects, Tasks, Team, Contributions, and System settings. I\'m also planning the Project Management UI with filtering options, archive functionality, templates, objectives, and an activity history. Then I\'m thinking about task and workflow management and adding Kanban, backlog, list, calendar, and timeline views.\n\n\n**Designing New UI Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating new features for enhanced team collaboration, building a dedicated `CollaborationPage.tsx` with tabs for meeting notes, discussions, peer recognition, and a daily stand-up generator. The collaboration features are under active development, and I\'ve started on an attachment section in the Jira issue detail modal for adding/downloading files. I\'m also planning to incorporate a dependency selector into the create/edit task modal, along with dependency badges.\n\n\n**Planning Project Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on project planning. I\'m adding a Milestones and Critical Path section to the Projects or Tasks page. I\'m planning sprint and milestone deadlines with progress meters and a critical path visualizer. This will highlight critical path tasks with estimated hours and schedule variance. I\'m also planning the contributions area, which will include a breakdown of contributions and dispute resolution.\n\nI\'m also working on team workload, where I\'m working on member skills badges and weekly capacity hours. I will also be working on the \"Smart Task Redistribution\" modal/panel.\n\n\n**Implementing Task Reassignment**\n\nI\'m now implementing 1-click \"Apply Reassignment\" functionality. I\'m focusing on smart task recommendations to match skills. Also, I\'m working on the Project Health Analytics and Risk Intelligence section, including a composite Project Health Score card with grades based on velocity and overdue ratios.\n\nI\'m incorporating a \"Ripple Effect & Bottleneck Simulator\" with an interactive slider to show impacts on sprint deadlines. In addition, I\'m integrating Quick Action Prompts in an AI Assistant Drawer, including daily standups and project health summaries. I\'m also planning project simulation and recovery options with what-if controls for deadline shifts and team capacity changes.\n\n\n**Adding Retrospective Insights**\n\nI\'m now integrating sprint retrospectives within `ReportsPage.tsx`, allowing logging and viewing of insights, including what went well and areas for improvement. I\'m also adding an \"Estimation Accuracy\" tab to generate charts showing the planned versus actual hours for individual tasks, as well as team averages.\n\nI\'m also working on dashboards and reporting features. I\'m incorporating a dashboard persona switcher in `DashboardPage.tsx` to include \"Executive / Manager View,\" \"My Work / Member View,\" and \"Admin View\" options.\n\n\n"
