  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Dashboard Features**\n\nI\'ve been examining the features within category 14, Dashboards & Reporting. The aim is to map them all out: Specifically, I\'m noting the: Project Manager, Team Member, Admin, Contribution, Risk, and Workload Heatmap dashboards. I\'m building a profile of the specific features.\n\n\n**Exploring New Dashboard Roles**\n\nI\'m now diving into enhancing the dashboard with user-specific roles. Specifically, I plan to add a selector at the top, enabling users to choose between a Project Manager view, a Team Member view, and an Admin/Organization Health perspective. I\'m imagining a persona-driven design where each role sees pertinent data. This involves adding the roles as selector items. My next step will be working on a heatmap matrix of member/project workload.\n\n\n**Implementing User Management Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating user profile management. I\'ve added the `onOpenProfile`, `onOpenInvitations`, and `onOpenRolePermissions` props to the `TopBar` component. I\'m adding buttons for \"Edit Profile & Credentials\", \"Team Member Invitations\", and \"Role Permissions Matrix\" to the user dropdown. Additionally, I\'ve imported several new modal components and created corresponding open/close states within `App.tsx`. I am also working on passing handler callbacks to `Sidebar` and `TopBar`.\n\n\n**Adding New Features**\n\nI\'m now focused on adding more features, including Contribution Type filter tabs like \"Testing & QA\" and \"Bug Fixes.\" I\'m also enhancing the Settings page with tabs for GitHub integration, custom contribution weights, and audit logs. I plan to wire up the custom weight sliders and audit log lists to their respective API calls. Finally, I\'m working on adding a persona toggle to the dashboard, including a workload heatmap and health indicators. I will wrap up by running the compile and lint verification.\n\n\n"
