  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User Request:** Build a dedicated, high-impact public Front/Landing Page displayed when the user first visits the application or when they log out. The top-right of the page must prominently feature the **\"Log In\"** and **\"Register\"** buttons (which open the existing authentication flows).\n- **Behavioral Flow:**\n  - If a user is not authenticated (or clicks \"Log Out\"), they land on this Front/Landing Page.\n  - The landing page header must display brand identity on the left and **Log In** & **Register** buttons on the top right.\n  - From the landing page, clicking \"Log In\" or \"Register\" opens `AuthModal` in the corresponding mode.\n  - An \"Explore Interactive Demo / Guest Access\" or \"Launch Workspace\" button allows immediate entry into the dashboard workspace.\n  - Once authenticated (or entering demo workspace mode), the app transitions into the main sidebar/dashboard view (`App.tsx`).\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed in Prior Turns:**\n  - Resolved all duplicate identifiers in `src/api/client.ts` (`resetPassword` consolidated polymorphically, duplicate `archiveProject` removed).\n  - Fixed `ConfirmDialogProps` in `src/components/common/ConfirmDialog.tsx` to accept `confirmText` as an alias alongside `confirmLabel`.\n  - Added missing `api` import to `src/components/tasks/TasksPage.tsx`.\n  - Fixed SQLite seed queries in `server.ts` where unquoted variables (`p1Id`, `m2Id`, `m4Id`) were causing SQL syntax errors; `/api/system/seed` executed successfully.\n  - Ran `tsc --noEmit` (`lint_applet`) and `compile_applet` (Vite build) \342\200\224 both pass with zero errors.\n  - Unit tests in `tests/github-parser.test.mjs` pass cleanly (3/3).\n  - Express + SQLite backend is healthy on port 3000.\n- **In Progress / Current Turn:**\n  - Designing and implementing the new `FrontPage` component (`src/components/landing/FrontPage.tsx` or similar) adhering to `frontend-design` guidelines (anti-slop, clean typography, WCAG AA, hero showcase, live metric counters, interactive platform previews, top-right Login & Register CTA buttons).\n  - Integrating `FrontPage` into `src/App.tsx` so unauthenticated visitors see the front page by default, and logging out returns them to it.\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- In `src/App.tsx`, authentication state is tracked via `user` (`User | null`) and `api.getStoredToken()` / `api.getMe()`.\n- Currently, if `user` is null or pending, it defaulted directly to displaying the dashboard with a guest fallback or opening the login modal.\n- Adding a dedicated `showFrontPage` state (or displaying the FrontPage whenever `!user && !isGuestDemo`) satisfies the requirement cleanly without breaking logged-in user experience.\n- `AuthModal` supports modes: `\'login\'`, `\'register\'`, and `\'reset\'`. The landing page can pass `initialMode=\"login\"` or `initialMode=\"register\"` to `onOpenAuth(mode)`.\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- **Dev Server:** Running on port 3000 via `server.ts` (`tsx server.ts`).\n- **Database:** SQLite in-memory with WAL pragma, fully seeded with sample projects (`p-ledger`, `p-portal`, `p-iam`), tasks, team members, discussions, kudos, and audit logs.\n- **Routing/State in `App.tsx`:** Manages `activeTab`, `currentUser`, and modal states (`isAuthModalOpen`, `authMode`).\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n1. **Create `src/components/landing/FrontPage.tsx`:**\n   - **Header:** Logo (\"Equinox\"), navigation anchors (Features, Architecture, Integrations, Metrics), and on the top right:\n     - `Log In` button (`onClick={() => onOpenAuth(\'login\')}`)\n     - `Register` / `Get Started` button (`onClick={() => onOpenAuth(\'register\')}`)\n   - **Hero Section:** Clear enterprise value proposition (\"Algorithmic Project Governance & Real-Time Contribution Auditing\"), interactive CTA (\"Launch Live Workspace\" / \"Sign In to Project\"), and a live interactive preview card showing real project velocity and Jira-linked commits.\n   - **Interactive Feature Showcases:**\n     - Real-Time Jira & GitHub commit hash synchronization.\n     - Invisible Work & Peer Recognition engine.\n     - What-If Cascading Ripple Simulator & single-point-of-failure detection.\n     - Granular Fair Contribution Ledger with algorithmic confidence scoring.\n   - **Social Proof & Stats Bar:** Real stats (e.g. 99.8% audit integrity, <12ms SQLite WAL queries, 0 duplicate ledger events).\n   - **Footer:** System status indicators, security compliance notes, and quick action links.\n2. **Update `src/App.tsx`:**\n   - Add state `isGuestPreview` or check if `user === null`: when logged out or on first load without a stored session, render `<FrontPage onOpenAuth={(mode) => ...} onExploreDemo={() => ...} />`.\n   - When user clicks \"Log Out\" in header/profile, set `user = null` and return to `FrontPage`.\n3. **Verify:**\n   - Run `lint_applet` and `compile_applet`.\n   - Verify dev server responsiveness and test the landing page -> login/register modal -> workspace transition.\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Top-right of front page **must** have both the **Login** and **Registration** buttons.\n- Front page must appear whenever the user first starts/opens the site (without an active session) and whenever they log out.\n- Strictly adhere to `frontend-design` constitution: avoid generic purple AI slop, no static pills for metadata, clean typographic hierarchy, and ensure all buttons have functional click handlers.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 246
    included_step_index_end: 335
    user_requests: "i want to create front page from the all which is show whenever the user is start the website and if the user log out they show that page and on the top of the page right side give the login and the registrtion button"
    render_latest_checkpoint: true
    total_subagent_count: 0
  }
