  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing App Logic**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `src/App.tsx`, specifically how authentication and the front page state are managed. I\'m noting that `loadAllData()` kicks things off with `api.getMe()`. If the response from that reveals a valid user session, I\'ll update `currentUser`.\n\n\n**Examining Flow Transitions**\n\nI\'ve mapped out the user flow. If a valid session exists at app load, the user goes straight to the dashboard. Otherwise, the front page renders, with a login modal available. I noticed how `handleAuthSuccess` sets `currentUser` and closes the modal, immediately transitioning the user. Logout resets everything, returning the user to the front page. Also, I analyzed the behavior of the guest user, by tracking how `isGuestPreview` works.\n\n\n"
