  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Front Page Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into `App.tsx` and focusing on the state management for the front page and workspace. My primary goal is to ensure a smooth transition between these two views. The user\'s requirement is clear: a front page on initial website load and after logout, always accessible at the top. I\'m considering various React state management approaches to achieve this seamless user experience.\n\n\n**Examining UI State Flow**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `App.tsx` file and pinpointed how `currentUser` and `isGuestPreview` states dictate the UI flow. Specifically, I see how the FrontPage and AuthModal are displayed based on these states. The plan is clearly defined: when a user logs in (or out), the corresponding state changes trigger the appropriate component mount/unmount and I\'ll need to figure out what to do with the workspace.\n\n\n**Clarifying Initial State**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that upon initial load and logout, the user is indeed directed to the Front Page. Furthermore, I\'ve outlined how to get back there for both authenticated users and guests, including an \"Exit Demo\" or \"Return to Front Page\" button in the `TopBar` and/or `Sidebar`. I am ensuring seamless UI changes. Also, I\'ve verified the `api.getMe()` function handles the initial token check, guaranteeing Front Page display when no valid token is present, and incorporated loading state handling.\n\n\n"
