  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining App State**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how `currentUser` and `isGuestPreview` will interact. I\'ve added state for `isGuestPreview` using `useState`. Now, I\'m thinking about the initial render. If there is no current user and no guest preview, I\'ll render the FrontPage and handle authentication. I think it makes sense to go with this.\n\n\n**Refining UI Flow**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a much clearer picture. I need to ensure the `AuthModal` is always rendered, so it\'s ready for login or registration. The `handleAuthSuccess` function will set the user, close the modal and exit the guest view. On logout, I\'ll clear the user, reset the guest state, close the modal, and take them back to the front page. Finally, the front page will include \"Log In\" and \"Register\" buttons.\n\n\n**Validating Authentication Flow**\n\nNow, I\'m streamlining the authentication process further. I realized that checking for a stored token upfront is key. If there\'s no token, we instantly go to the `FrontPage`. If there is a token, we can show a brief loading state while `api.getMe()` validates. If successful, we go to the workspace; otherwise, clear the token and show the `FrontPage`. This eliminates unnecessary waits and ensures a smooth user experience.\n\n\n"
