    thinking: "**Refining TopBar Implementation**\n\nI\'m currently updating the `TopBar.tsx` component. I\'ve considered adding `onOpenFrontPage` (a function) and `isGuestPreview` (a boolean) to the `TopBarProps`. When `onOpenFrontPage` is defined, I\'m thinking of incorporating a button within the breadcrumb section of the TopBar.\n\n\n**Adding UI Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating new UI elements into the `TopBar` based on user state. Specifically, if a user isn\'t logged in, I\'m adding \"Log In\" and \"Register\" buttons directly to the `TopBar`. I\'m using `onOpenAuth` function with arguments, to handle opening the authentication modal, depending on which button gets clicked. This provides a quick access for users that are not logged in.\n\n\n**Integrating Front Page Access**\n\nI\'m now focusing on adding a \"Return to Front Page\" button to the user profile dropdown within the `TopBar`. I\'ve incorporated this conditionally, only if `onOpenFrontPage` is provided. This uses an `ExternalLink` icon and correctly closes the user menu before executing the provided function to return to the front page.\n\n\n"
