  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Project Leader Logic**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `handleCreateProject` function within `App.tsx`. I\'m working to ensure the `leader_id` is correctly set. If a user is logged in, their ID should be automatically assigned. I need to make sure the logic handles the case where no user is logged in gracefully. I\'m evaluating the best method to ensure consistent and secure project leadership assignment.\n\n\n**Refining Leadership Assignments**\n\nI\'ve refined the leadership assignment logic. The `handleCreateProject` function in `App.tsx` now correctly leverages the server-side assignment. On the server, I\'ve implemented a robust approach to assign leaders based on the user\'s authentication status, handling the \'no user\' scenario gracefully. I\'ve also implemented a `transfer-leadership` route, providing a clear transfer feature. This includes verification, role updates, and audit logging.\n\n\n**Implementing Leadership Transfer Features**\n\nI\'ve just added complete functionality for transferring project leadership. I\'ve integrated a robust `transferProjectLeadership` function, complete with audit logging, and appropriate user notifications. I\'ve added a dedicated \"Transfer Leadership\" action within the project view, along with confirmation dialogs. A key aspect is the `api.transferProjectLeadership(projectId, memberId)` call, and its effects on notifications and project updates. Also, I\'ve incorporated leader transfer into the role selection dropdown.\n\n\n**Adjusting User Role Management**\n\nI\'m currently updating the `SystemRole` type definition in `src/types/index.ts` to include \'Team Leader\' and \'Member\'. I\'m also ensuring backward compatibility with \'Admin\' and \'Manager\' through helper functions. In `server.ts`, I\'ve updated the seed user roles and modified the registration route to default to \'Member\', but allow for explicit \'Team Leader\' designation. I\'m updating role checks to prioritize \'Team Leader\' and incorporate backward-compatible checks for legacy roles. Finally, I\'m modifying the role dropdown in `AuthModal.tsx` to reflect the updated options.\n\n\n"
