  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Consolidating Roles\' Permissions**\n\nI\'ve successfully run the linter; the code appears clean. Now, I\'m diving into the requirements. First up, I\'m focusing on Requirement 1: the integration of Manager and Admin roles into a single Team Leader role. I am starting to map out how to combine all the existing permissions and responsibilities.\n\n\n**Reviewing Remaining Requirements**\n\nI\'ve just reviewed the remaining requirements. I\'m taking a close look at updating the Login and Sign-Up pages. I will remove the separate \"Reset Password\" section, and I will be adding a \"Forgot Password?\" link. After that, I will review the Team Leader permissions. Lastly, I will be working on how Team Members will be able to track their work status.\n\n\n**Defining Team Leader Permissions**\n\nI\'m now detailing the changes needed. First, in `src/types/index.ts`, I\'m updating `TaskStatus` and `SystemRole`. Then, I\'ll update the server side to update existing user roles to Team Leader, seed with Team Leader users, and ensure tasks use the standardized statuses. The overall goal is to merge Admin and Manager roles.\n\n\n**Clarifying Leader Functions**\n\nI\'m now detailing the implications of consolidating roles. I am thinking through default user roles upon registration. Should it be \'Team Leader\' or \'Member\'? Also, I have detailed how leadership should be handled in Project Creation, and the appropriate endpoints for transferring leadership, including assigning proper statuses in `project_members`. Finally, I\'m working through updating tasks in the status update endpoint.\n\n\n**Implementing Task Status Updates**\n\nI\'m now implementing the task status update endpoint, `PATCH /api/tasks/:id/status`. It validates the status, normalizing \"To Do\" to \"Not Started\" and \"Done\" to \"Completed.\" I\'m also adding audit logs and notifications for completed tasks. Next, I\'m working on the endpoint for tracking member work status, which includes total tasks, status counts, progress percentage, and task details. I\'ll need to figure out whether to place this endpoint at `/api/team/work-status` or `/api/projects/:id/work-status`.\n\n\n**Refining Login/Signup Flow**\n\nI\'m currently working on the user interface for password resets and registrations. I\'ve integrated the \"Forgot Password?\" link into the login page using the code you see above. For password reset mode, I\'ve defined a clear layout with the header, subtitle, email, and password fields, and submit button. I am also working on the registration form to include the Team Leader and Team Member roles, and I\'m adding a role permissions modal and updating the settings page to reflect the role consolidations. I am now working on fast demo profiles to align with the permissions.\n\n\n**Updating Role Descriptions**\n\nI\'ve updated the user profile modal and project leader modal, and I am focusing on the user interface. I\'m clarifying role options to reflect that team leaders have full system, project, and team leadership, while members are team members or developers. I\'m adding a project leader badge and a \"Transfer Leadership\" button on project cards and in the project leader modal. I\'m also implementing a confirmation prompt to ensure that transferring leadership includes all associated permissions. I\'m focusing on the implementation details now.\n\n\n**Visualizing Task Statuses**\n\nI am now visualizing task statuses and workflows. I\'ve standardized on \"Not Started,\" \"In Progress,\" and \"Completed.\" I\'m updating Kanban board columns and drag-and-drop actions to reflect these statuses. I am working on how the status filter dropdowns and quick action modals for task cards also adhere to these statuses. I am also working on adding a \"Team Member Work Status Tracking\" panel in `TeamPage.tsx` and `DashboardPage.tsx`.\n\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1162441"
