  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Endpoint Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the functionality of the `transfer-leadership` endpoint. Right now, I\'m going over Requirement 3, regarding Team Leader permissions, to ensure alignment. The endpoint should handle the leader transfer, with consideration to the permissions requirements.\n\n\n**Implementing Transfer Logic**\n\nI\'ve moved on to implementing the transfer logic for the `transfer-leadership` endpoint. I\'m starting by constructing the basic route and error handling, including checks for project existence and a valid `new_leader_id`. I\'m using queries to look up potential team members or users. Currently, I am querying the database for a potential match on an ID.\n\n\n**Refining Leader Transfer**\n\nI\'m now refining the leader transfer implementation. I\'m focusing on the database updates, especially ensuring a smooth transition. Specifically, I\'m working through the logic to demote the previous leader and also to correctly update project memberships. I have introduced logic to identify the correct user from a potential match. I am also working through scenarios for potential errors during execution.\n\n\n**Finalizing Updates**\n\nI\'m wrapping up the database updates for leader transfers. I\'ve ensured smooth transitions, demoting the previous leader and properly updating project memberships. I\'ve incorporated logic to identify users correctly, including checking for matches between user and team member, considering email. I am ensuring that the `users` table is updated with the correct role. Finally, I\'m integrating the audit log for record-keeping.\n\n\n**Announcing the Transfer**\n\nI\'m now implementing the announcement system after a successful leader transfer. I\'m focusing on sending a notification to the new leader, confirming their new role and the project name. I\'ve also incorporated the updated project information and a confirmation message in the response.\n\n\n"
